            "review_title": "Review at Thiem Huy Mi Gia",
            "review_text": "esCape2\nKuala Lumpur, Malaysia40 contributions\n0\nCantonese Cuisine / Black Chicken Herbal Soup\nDec 2019 • Couples\nIf one is craving for Cantonese cuisine after a few days of local Vietnamese foods, this restaurant would probably satisfy more than your need. We ordered fried duck-meat soup noodle, black chicken herbal soup and tim-sum (siew-mai) for our lunch when we visited this place. Their foods were excellent esp the siew-mai with fresh crunchy shrimp filling, and the herbal soup was quite good and authentic. Good place to visit if one is within the vicinity!\nRead more\nWritten January 3, 2020",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-13",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
